    "gross_loss": 48272.0,
    "cushion_points_of_gross_loss": 4.957946635730858,
    "notes": "New Style JSA is contribution-based and paid for a maximum of 182 days (26 weeks) at the standard personal allowance for claimants aged 25 or over. The figure is the MAXIMUM contribution-based entitlement over a full displacement spell for a representative displaced worker on the exposed-sector mean wage, expressed as percentage points of that worker's gross earnings loss. It is an UPPER BOUND on the net addition to cushioning for two reasons: New Style JSA is taxable, and it is deducted pound for pound from any Universal Credit award, so a displaced family already receiving UC gains nothing from it. It also assumes the claimant satisfies the class 1 contribution conditions and claims for the full 182 days. Reported to show the scale of an omitted institution, not as an estimate of what NS-JSA would add."
  },
